<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania 91-day T-bill rate slips lower.</title>
<headline>Lithuania 91-day T-bill rate slips lower.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on 91-day Lithuanian T-bills slipped to 10.01 percent on Tuesday from 10.50 percent at an auction on Monday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV YIELD  LAST TIME  MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID    SOLD</p>
<p>  91-day    10.01     10.50     9.70/10.28  40   80.398   40</p>
<p>The settlement date for the auction is February 28, and the</p>
<p>bills mature on May 30.</p>
<p>The next auction is on March 3 when 50 million litas ($12.5 million) of 92-day paper will be on sale and on March 4 when 50 million litas of 182-day bills be offered for sale.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240 ($ = 3.997 Lithuanian Litas)</p>
